{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PrincipalSchurHook","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HookDivisibility"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.coeff_fmaj_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.coeff_fmaj_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L434-L436","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.coeff_fmaj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.coeff_fmaj","kind":"theorem","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L425-L432","doc":"The coefficients of `f_μ` count standard tableaux by `maj`; in particular they are `≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.qFactorial_eq_schurElt_mul_fmaj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.qFactorial_eq_schurElt_mul_fmaj","kind":"theorem","line":411,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L411-L423","doc":"**`[n]_Q! / c_λ(Q)` is the `maj` generating function.**  For `Q ≠ 0, 1` in a field,\n`[n]_Q! = c_λ(Q) · ∑_{S ∈ SYT(λ)} Q^{maj S}`.  So `[n]_Q!/c_λ` is a polynomial in `Q` with\nnonnegative integer coefficients (`coeff_fmaj`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.fmaj_mul_qHook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.fmaj_mul_qHook","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L397-L408","doc":"**The `maj` formula in `q`-integers**: `f_μ · ∏_c [h(c)] = X^{n(μ)} · [n]!` in `ℤ[X]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.fmaj_mul_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.fmaj_mul_hook","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L347-L392","doc":"**The `maj` formula** (Stanley, *EC2* Cor. 7.21.5), division-free:\n\n`(∑_{S ∈ SYT(μ)} X^{maj S}) · ∏_{c ∈ μ} (1 − X^{h(c)}) = X^{n(μ)} · ∏_{m=1}^{|μ|} (1 − X^m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.one_sub_X_pow_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.one_sub_X_pow_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L342-L345","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.eExp_eq_nPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.eExp_eq_nPart","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L327-L340","doc":"`e(μ) = ∑_{j<N} j · μ_j` is `n(μ) = ∑_{c ∈ μ} c₁` once `N` covers every row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.fmaj_rowYD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.fmaj_rowYD","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MajFormula.lean#L317-L323","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.SYTe.e_rowYD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MajFormula.SYTe.e_rowYD","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/734